---
description: Documentation and ADR rules for CircleSfera — keep docs true to the code
globs: circlesfera-documentation/**, CHANGELOG.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, .ai/**, .agents/**, AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: false
---

If the system and the documentation disagree, classify the conflict before fixing either side — see
`.ai/core/authority.md`: stale documentation → correct it; code that no longer follows a valid
normative decision → treat as a candidate defect, don't rewrite the documentation to legitimize it;
two authoritative sources disagreeing → stop and escalate; insufficient evidence → verify before
deciding.

- Verify every factual statement against the canonical artifact before writing it: `schema.prisma` for
  data, controllers for endpoints, the owning service for business rules,
  `circlesfera-frontend/src/index.css` for tokens, the workflows and compose files for deployment, the
  relevant `package.json` for versions.
- Never paste canonical content. Link to it. That is why `08-schema-prisma.md` is only a pointer.
- Present tense means shipped. Mark planned work explicitly — `11-backups-strategy.md` deliberately
  separates shipped scripts from aspirational WAL/PITR, and that labelling must stay.
- Numbered product docs are `00`–`15`. Prefer schema and controllers when they disagree with narrative
  docs; check `00-status.md` for freshness.
- Cross-references use plain section numbers (`section 9.4`, `sections 3.5 and 3.11`) — never the `§`
  symbol.
- Docs `09` and `13` are Notion-canonical for design/UI — do not rewrite them from CSS memory; prefer
  `index.css` for shipped tokens (see `.ai/core/known-gaps.md` D3).
- A durable decision with alternatives and consequences belongs in an ADR:
  `circlesfera-documentation/adr/NNNN-slug.md`, numbered next in sequence and added to the table in
  `adr/README.md`. Template: `.ai/templates/adr.md`.
- Operational procedures belong in `circlesfera-documentation/runbooks/`.
- `CHANGELOG.md` follows Keep a Changelog; user- and operator-visible changes go under `[Unreleased]`
  and describe impact, not internal mechanics.
- `.ai/` is derived context, never canonical. Every file there declares its source and verification
  date.
- Drift you find but do not fix goes in `.ai/core/known-gaps.md` with evidence and a risk note. Do not
  silently rewrite documents you were not asked to touch.
- Never document an endpoint, model, enum or flow that does not exist in code. Never mark a document
  final when it rests on assumptions.
- `circlesfera-landing/` was removed from the tree (Jul 2026). Do not document it as active or restore it.

Full process: @.ai/playbooks/docs-sync.md
